  "resolvedValidationFindings": [
    "Discarded iframe timers stranded effect/reset settlements: retirement now flushes queued results, with deterministic and real iframe-removal tests.",
    "Diagnostic-listener reentry could interrupt state mutation: ordinary state notifications now use microtasks; final retirement notifications publish synchronously after invalidation, suppressing queued stale playing output.",
    "Firefox WebDriver sandbox Promise differs from page Promise: assertions use the actual binding realm constructors; child conversion-error realm and caller exception identity are checked.",
    "Firefox startup fixture attached input listeners after async setup and could miss added events: moved listener attachment before setup, preserving the existing assertion. Full Firefox suite subsequently passed.",
    "Firefox drawWindow capture omitted the remote panel: replaced it with a direct WindowGlobalParent.drawSnapshot capture and inspected the resulting haptic readout pixels.",
    "The inherited full Chromium failure reproduced on the unchanged upstream archive. Corrected XRInputSource and XRFrame public ancestry to use their owning document Object.prototype while retaining the shared private brands and constructor permissions. The existing events and bulk-frame assertions now pass; both browser hand provenance suites also pass.",
    "Updated smoke fixtures that assumed XRSystem.devicePromise was public or that constructing CustomWebXRPolyfill created a fresh runtime. The profile wait reuses the existing held-session adapter observation; deferred tests now hold the genuine init event in a fresh injected document, preserving all conversion/resource assertions.",
    "Compared XRRay direction components by numeric equality so valid signed zeros are accepted; origin and all direction components remain checked exactly. This changes the harness, not ray behavior."
  ],
